## Risk Factors

> [!WARNING]
> **LLM API Costs**: Autonomous agent will make many LLM calls. Need to:
> - Implement cost tracking/estimation before execution
> - Add cost limits in settings
> - Use cheaper models where possible (Claude Haiku, GPT-4o-mini)

> [!CAUTION]
> **Agent Reliability**: Autonomous agent may:
> - Get stuck in loops
> - Generate incorrect plans
> - Consume excessive resources
> - Need robust error handling and kill switches

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Scope Creep Risk**: The autonomous agent is a large feature. Consider implementing in iterations:
> - v1: Manual tool execution (user approves each step)
> - v2: Semi-autonomous (user approves plan, agent executes)
> - v3: Fully autonomous (agent plans and executes)

---

## Notes

- Phase 2 now focuses on UI before model management because the new UI structure is needed first
- The autonomous agent is the biggest new feature and spans 2 phases
- LLM integration is critical path for autonomous features
- Consider feature flags to ship iteratively
- The original GalaxyCanvas 3D visualization has been removed in favor of the cleaner desktop UI
